𝐂𝐚𝐫𝐥 𝐂𝐚𝐫𝐥𝐭𝐨𝐧 (𝐌𝐚𝐲 𝟐𝟏, 𝟏𝟗𝟓𝟑 – 𝐃𝐞𝐜𝐞𝐦𝐛𝐞𝐫 𝟏𝟒, 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟓) ⁣𝐂𝐚𝐫𝐥 𝐂𝐚𝐫𝐥𝐭𝐨𝐧 𝐝𝐢𝐝𝐧’𝐭 𝐣𝐮𝐬𝐭 𝐬𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐚𝐛𝐨𝐮𝐭 𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐥𝐚𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐥𝐨𝐯𝐞 — 𝐡𝐞 𝐥𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐝 𝐢𝐭 𝐭𝐡𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐠𝐡 𝐡𝐢𝐬 𝐯𝐨𝐢𝐜𝐞. 𝐋𝐨𝐧𝐠 𝐚𝐟𝐭𝐞𝐫 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐦𝐮𝐬𝐢𝐜 𝐟𝐚𝐝𝐞𝐬, 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐦𝐭𝐡, 𝐬𝐨𝐮𝐥 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐡𝐮𝐦𝐚𝐧𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐢𝐧 𝐡𝐢𝐬 𝐬𝐨𝐧𝐠𝐬 𝐰𝐢𝐥𝐥 𝐜𝐨𝐧𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐮𝐞 𝐭𝐨 𝐫𝐞𝐦𝐢𝐧𝐝 𝐮𝐬 𝐡𝐨𝐰 𝐝𝐞𝐞𝐩𝐥𝐲 𝐨𝐧𝐞 𝐯𝐨𝐢𝐜𝐞 𝐜𝐚𝐧 𝐭𝐨𝐮𝐜𝐡 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐰𝐨𝐫𝐥𝐝. Album: Everlasting Love  -  Released in 1974. Songwriters: Mac Gayden and Buzz Cason [Gayden died April 16, 2025, from complications of Parkinson's disease; age of 83 and Cason died June 16, 2024: age of 84]. The original version of "Everlasting Love" was recorded in Nashville by Robert Knight, whose producers/writers Buzz Cason and Mac Gayden aimed to record him in a Motown style. Ultimately "Everlasting Love" was released as an A-side for Knight and reached #13 in 1967. Subsequently, the song has reached the US Top 40 three times, most successfully by Carl Carlton, who peaked at #6 in 1974.  Carl Carlton is an American artist who sings R&B, soul and funk. Born in Detroit, Michigan on May 21 in 1953, he started his career during the 1960s when he was still a kid. In 1968, he signed a contract with Back Beat Records, after which he moved to Texas.. In the early 70’s music era he achieved his biggest hit with “Everlasting Love” which became a Top 10 pop hit single and oldies music classic.                                                                                                                                         

Presenter of Soul Train: Donald Cortez (Don) Cornelius (Chicago (Illinois), September 27, 1936 - Sherman Oaks (California), died: February 1, 2012). Cornelius was found dead in his Los Angeles home at the age of 75. The presenter was found to have succumbed to a gunshot wound to the head as a result of a suicide attempt. Below: Continuation of health problems and depression Don Cornelius.

The immense popularity of the song lies in its flexibility; it could be adapted to various genres, from soul and pop to rock, country, and dance. Also covered by :
U2, Jamie Cullum,The Love Affair, The Ravers, MFP Studio Artists, Hank Locklin, James Last, David Ruffin ,The Senate, The Sonic, Kings Road, The Hiltonaires, Solomon Burke, Patricia Paay, Louise Mandrell, Narvel Felts, Soirée, The Kendalls, Rex Smith and Rachel Sweet, The Truth, Sandra (Germany), David Essex, Worlds Apart, Gloria Estefan, Stanford Harmonics, Seventh Avenue Party Animals, The Cast from Casualty, Reverse Osmosis, På Slaget 12, Mysterio Scooter, Kerry Norton, Michael Ball, The Soldiers, Manuel, etc. 

